    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, quick question for the year end reports. we bought a CNC milling machine for $85,000 earlier this year. the useful life is estimated at 7 years and we expect a salvage value of $5,000 at the end of that. can you walk me through the straight-line depreciation calculation for the first year? thanks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The straight-line depreciation formula is (Cost - Salvage Value) / Useful Life. Plugging in your numbers, you calculate $(\\$85,000 - \\$5,000) / 7$ years. This results in an annual depreciation expense of $\\$12,142.86$. Therefore, the depreciation for the first year of the CNC machine is $\\$12,142.86$.",
      "source": "target",
