      "content": "Since the depreciation is straight-line, you simply multiply the annual depreciation by the number of years. After 4 years, the accumulated depreciation will be $4 \\times \\$12,142.86$, which equals $\\$48,571.44$. To find the book value, subtract this accumulated depreciation from the original cost: $\\$85,000 - \\$48,571.44$. Thus, the book value of the machine after four years would be $\\$36,428.56$.",
      "source": "target",
